course: dictionary
lesson: 11973
title: Careful and slow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone does something. «Cautiously» is one of them. It is an adverb, so it describes an action. Ask yourself: how did they move, speak or act?
explain: «Mia looked both ways and crossed the road cautiously.» Looking both ways is careful, so cautiously means carefully, to avoid danger. «The fox crept cautiously into the dark cave» shows a fox that is wary and slow, not sure what is inside.
explain: The word can also show doubt. «The doctor was cautiously hopeful that the patient would get better.» Hopeful means she felt good about it, but cautiously tells you she was not yet fully sure. Read the clues around the word, then swap in your meaning to check it fits.
fact: Cautiously is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Cautiously» means carefully, so as to avoid danger or mistakes.
fact: «Cautiously» can also mean slowly and not fully trusting something yet, as in «cautiously hopeful».
fact: «Cautiously optimistic» means hopeful but not sure.
fact: The comparative form is more cautiously, as in «She walked more cautiously after she slipped.»
exercise: «Sam held the hot pan cautiously, using both hands.» What does cautiously mean here? | Happily | Loudly | Carelessly and fast | *Carefully, so as to avoid getting hurt
exercise: «The cat crept cautiously towards the strange box.» What does cautiously suggest about the cat? | It is bored and asleep | It is very fast and angry | It is sure of everything | *It is wary and careful
exercise: The news says «cautiously optimistic». What does this mean? | Happy and sure | *Hopeful, but not completely sure | Angry and loud | Certain that everything will go wrong
test: «She opened the letter cautiously, afraid of what it might say.» What does cautiously tell you about how she opened it? | *Carefully, because she was worried | Without looking | Quickly and happily | Loudly
test: Which word means nearly the same as cautiously, as in «He walked cautiously across the icy path»? | Rudely | Brightly | Fast | *Carefully
exam: «The children stepped cautiously onto the thin ice.» What does cautiously mean? | Very fast | *Slowly and carefully, to avoid danger | Happily | Without any care
